```

### 9. Don’t forget unhandled rejections and signal handling

A mis‑behaving promise can bring the whole process crashing. Add a global handler:

```js
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason, promise) => {
  log.error('Unhandled Rejection at:', promise, 'reason:', reason);
  // Depending on the policy – shut down cleanly
  process.exit(1);
});

process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  log.info('SIGTERM received. Shutting down.');
  process.exit(0); // or gracefully close the server
});
```

### 10. Extract the router logic to a separate module

Keeping all routes in a single file makes it harder to audit. With separation:

```js
// routes/users.js
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();

router.get('/', async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
