## 2. Security‑Focused Improvement Checklist

> **Tip:** Begin with these, then layer on more advanced controls as your app grows.

| Category | Recommendation | Reason | Sample Code |
|----------|----------------|--------|-------------|
| **Transport Layer** | Use HTTPS. | Prevent man‑in‑the‑middle & eavesdropping. | *Not in Express preview – handled by reverse proxy.* |
| **Environment Variables** | Move port & secret keys to `process.env`. | Secrets stay out of source. | `const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;` |
| **Express Middleware** | `helmet()` – inject many protective headers. | Mitigates click‑jacking, MIME sniffing, XSS, etc. | `app.use(helmet());` |
| **Input Validation** | Even for the `/health` endpoint, guard against path traversal / unnatural requests. | Preparation for future routes that expect params. | `const Joi = require('@hapi/joi');`<br>`const schema = Joi.object({ id: Joi.number().integer().positive().required() });` |
| **Rate Limiting** | `express-rate-limit` or `rate-limiter-flexible`. | Stop brute‐force & DoS. | `app.use(limiter);` |
| **Error Handling** | Dedicated error handling middleware that never leaks stack traces. | Prevent info disclosure. | `app.use((err, req, res, next) => { /* sanitized */ });` |
| **CORS** | Explicitly configure allowed origins. | Reduce MIME‑type flipping & accidental data exposes. | `app.use(cors({ origin: 'https://trusteddomain.com' }));` |
| **Content Security Policy** | With `helmet.contentSecurityPolicy`. | Mitigate XSS. | `helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({ directives: { ... } });` |
| **Input Sanitization** | Use `express-mongo-sanitize` if you’re passing data to Mongo, or `xss-clean`. | Prevent NoSQL injection, XSS. | `app.use(mongoSanitize());` |
| **Logging** | Use `morgan` + structured logs. | Better observability & correlation. | `app.use(morgan('combined'));` |
| **Graceful Shutdown** | Capture SIGTERM/SIGINT and close DB connections, etc. | Avoid broken connections on restart/scale‑up. | `process.on('SIGTERM', gracefulShutdown);` |
| **Unit Tests** | Write tests for new validation & error handling. | Catch regressions. | *No code snippet – use Jest or Mocha.* |

